# Wave W17-N (Mt. Smokestack): smoke turf — ash-dusted summit grass: the slope green dulled under a permanent grey creep of ash at its edges, pale ash flecks standing in it like the fall the researchers log (design: calm speckled grass failing into ash and warm rock on a volcano summit; the ash here is data with a smell). The Summit’s own ground — greyer and thinner than Route 112’s warm slope grass below, and split from Route 113’s swept ash road by register: this ash FALLS here, unswept, on living grass.
